#: ../../../topics/downloader-middleware.rst:163
msgid "Downloading a request from a downloader middleware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/downloader-middleware.rst:165
msgid ""
"A downloader middleware can download a request of its own while it processes "
"another one, e.g. to fetch something that the request it is processing "
"needs. The built-in :ref:`robots.txt middleware <topics-dlmw-robots>` does "
"that: it holds each request while it downloads the ``robots.txt`` file of "
"its website."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/downloader-middleware.rst:170
msgid ""
"Use :meth:`crawler.engine.download_async() <scrapy.core.engine."
"ExecutionEngine.download_async>` for that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/downloader-middleware.rst:173
msgid ""
"from scrapy import Request\n"
"from scrapy.http.request import NO_CALLBACK\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class TokenMiddleware:\n"
"    def __init__(self, crawler):\n"
"        self.crawler = crawler\n"
"        self.token = None\n"
"\n"
"    @classmethod\n"
"    def from_crawler(cls, crawler):\n"
"        return cls(crawler)\n"
"\n"
"    async def process_request(self, request):\n"
"        if request.meta.get(\"dont_obey_robotstxt\"):\n"
"            return\n"
"        if self.token is None:\n"
"            response = await self.crawler.engine.download_async(\n"
"                Request(\n"
"                    \"https://example.com/token\",\n"
"                    callback=NO_CALLBACK,\n"
"                    meta={\"dont_obey_robotstxt\": True},\n"
"                )\n"
"            )\n"
"            self.token = response.text\n"
"        request.headers[\"Authorization\"] = self.token"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/downloader-middleware.rst:202
msgid ""
"Requests that you download this way go through the downloader middleware "
"chain as well, including your own middleware and the :ref:`robots.txt "
"middleware <topics-dlmw-robots>`, which holds a request until the ``robots."
"txt`` file of its website arrives. Be careful not to introduce deadlocks: a "
"request that you download must not end up waiting for the request that is "
"waiting for it. Hence :reqmeta:`dont_obey_robotstxt` above, which makes both "
"middlewares let the token request through."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/downloader-middleware.rst:210
msgid ""
"While the first token response is in transit, ``process_request`` runs for "
"other requests as well, and the middleware above downloads a token for each "
"of them. Cache the task that downloads the token, and not only its result, "
"to download the token only once."
msgstr ""

